Debug-only instrumentation for the armv7 SIGBUS investigation.

Adds:
  1) A SIGBUS handler installed at the top of nxt_router_start() that
     prints si_addr, PC, LR, SP, and r0..r7 from ucontext_t before the
     router child dies.  Resolve PC with:
       addr2line -e build/sbin/unitd -fC 0x<pc>
  2) dprintf() bisect markers around the two sub-calls inside
     nxt_http_init() so the test log identifies which sub-init traps
     even if the handler output is truncated.

No abort().  No behavioural change beyond stderr writes and the
SIGBUS handler.  Drop before merging any fix.

Pair with the UBSan CFLAGS hunk described in apkbuild.snippet for the
strongest signal under clang-22 + musl + qemu-user.

